       'Matt 24:45-51''s faithful-and-wise-servant vs evil-servant substance — the substantial-stewardship-substance the King walks against the substantial-inherited-Reformation-eternal-security-substance — read against the wisdom-stream''s articulation of the reward-according-to-works + post-harvest-sifting + day-of-visitation architecture in Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) and Wisdom of Solomon. Four moves: Sirach 11:26 names the direct verbal-anchor for the reward-according-to-his-ways substance (*for it is an easy thing to Yahuah (God) in the day of death to reward a man according to his ways*) the substantial-faithful-and-wise-servant walks-into at Matt 24:46; Sirach 16:14 names the every-man-shall-find-according-to-his-works substance the substantial-greater-stewardship-substance at Matt 24:47 walks-the-architecture-of (*make him ruler over all his goods*); Sirach 27:4 names the substantial-post-harvest-sifting architecture (*as when one sifteth with a sieve, the refuse remains*) the substantial-evil-servant at Matt 24:51 walks-the-judgment-substance of — the substance the prophet-Yechezk''el (Ezekiel) walked at Ezekiel 18:24 (*when the righteous turneth away from his righteousness... all his righteousness that he hath done shall not be mentioned*) — ties-back to the substantial Matthew 23 seven-woes-against-the-hypocrites the evil-servant walks-the-same-substance-as the substantial-Pharisaic-Sadducean-leadership had-walked; Wisdom of Solomon 3:7 names the time-of-visitation substance (*in the time of their visitation they shall shine, and run to and fro like sparks among the stubble*) the substantial-faithful-and-wise-servant at Matt 24:46 walks-the-shining-substance-of in continuity with Daniel 12:3 + Matthew 13:43. The framework reads the cluster against the substantial-inherited-Reformation-eternal-security-substance — the substantial-substance is not the substantial-one-time-confession-substance but the substantial-walking-out-of-the-substantial-works the substantial-Spirit-internalized-Torah-substance walks per the substantial-new-heart-of-Yechezk''el (Ezekiel) 36:26-27, the substantial-grace as the substantial-door-home opened-by-the-substantial-categorically-exempt-One''s-voluntary-walking-into-the-shameful-death the substantial-categorically-bound owed, with the substantial-consequences-of-walking-off-the-substantial-Way still-real because the substantial-Way is-real per *Grace, the Way, the New Heart, and the Mercy of Depart*.',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'complete_study', 345
  FROM _s156_xref_lookup sv, _s156_xref_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug = 'canon' AND sv.book_slug = 'matthew' AND sv.chapter_number = 24 AND sv.verse_number = 45
